# Android emulators on this Mac

Prefer physical phones (`docs/install.md`). The Mac overheats with long CLI emulator
boots and dual-AVD runs.

## Current AVDs

- **Pixel_XL**: API 29 `google_apis` — the stable guest for scripts.
- **Pixel_9a**: Android 16 (API 36) `google_apis_playstore`, skin `pixel_9a`,
  `hw.device.name=pixel_9` (avdmanager has no `pixel_9a` device id), `hw.gpu.mode=auto`, **3-button navigation** (required, see below).
  Device Manager must show API 36, not 0. A wrong `target` (e.g. `android-36.1` with old
  cmdline-tools) shows as **API 0**.

## Do / don't

- Start AVDs from **Device Manager** when possible; let Play first boot finish.
- If Pixel_9a bootloops, check `adb logcat -b crash` first. The 2026-11-12 loop looked like
  a killed first boot but was the gesture-navigation crash below; wiping would not have
  fixed it.
- Pixel_9a must stay on **3-button navigation**. With gesture navigation, emulator 37.2.13
  with the API 36 Play image crash-loops: SurfaceFlinger `RegionSampling` aborts on
  `hasReadColorBufferDma`, taking the launcher and system_server down every ~10 s. It
  happens with every GPU mode (`auto`, `host`, software) and with `GLDMA`/`GLDMA2` off, so
  GPU flags and wiping data do not fix it. After a wipe or recreate, set it again while
  the device loops:
  `adb shell cmd overlay enable-exclusive --category com.android.internal.systemui.navbar.threebutton`
  then `adb emu avd snapshot save default_boot` so quick boot does not reload the bad state.
- Do **not** leave Play Store first boots running unattended in CLI; kill qemu if the Mac
  heats up.
- AOSP `default` is stable but looks wrong (no Pixel UI). Play / `google_apis` for UI.
- Dual-emu LAN: scripts exist; expect flakiness. Prefer phone↔phone or one emu + iOS sim.
